# Local addressing for mac-dev-playbook — COPY this file to `.env` and fill it in.
# NEVER commit `.env`; it is gitignored and on the sanitization deny-list.
#
# Addresses ONLY — no credentials (F10). Router keys (LITELLM_MASTER_KEY, virtual
# keys) live in the router package's own .env on Unraid + 1Password, never here.
#
# Keys are per-host, hostname UPPER_SNAKE_CASE prefixed (the inventory alias
# `mac-headless` -> `MAC_HEADLESS`). Under G30 = LAN, inference binds and the
# LiteLLM api_base use *_LAN_IP (set static DHCP reservations matching the
# router's M1PRO_IP/M4PRO_IP). Tailscale IP/name are for SSH/management only.
#
# Placeholder values below use RFC 5737 (192.0.2.x) and the CGNAT range Tailscale
# uses (100.64.x.x); replace them all. Back this file up (1Password secure note
# or the private Gitea mirror) — losing it re-creates the address archaeology.

# Optional per-host SSH keys drive the CONNECTION (see group_vars/all.yml):
#   MAC_<HOST>_SSH_USER   set  -> that host is driven over SSH (remote), as this
#                                 user, to MAC_<HOST>_SSH_HOST or its _LAN_IP.
#   MAC_<HOST>_SSH_USER   unset -> connection=local (run ON the box). DEFAULT.
#   MAC_<HOST>_SSH_HOST   optional override for the SSH target (e.g. a Tailscale
#                                 name for off-LAN management); defaults to _LAN_IP.
# Put these ONLY in the .env of the CONTROL node that drives the remote — not in
# the .env on the box itself (or it would try to SSH to itself).

# --- mac-headless ---
MAC_HEADLESS_LAN_IP=192.0.2.10
MAC_HEADLESS_TAILNET_IP=100.64.0.10
MAC_HEADLESS_TAILNET_NAME=mac-headless.tailnet-example.ts.net
# MAC_HEADLESS_SSH_USER=youruser          # uncomment on the control node to drive it remotely
# MAC_HEADLESS_SSH_HOST=192.0.2.10        # optional; defaults to MAC_HEADLESS_LAN_IP

# --- mac-personal ---
MAC_PERSONAL_LAN_IP=192.0.2.11
MAC_PERSONAL_TAILNET_IP=100.64.0.11
MAC_PERSONAL_TAILNET_NAME=mac-personal.tailnet-example.ts.net

# --- mac-work ---  (work Macs never serve inference; addresses optional)
# MAC_WORK_LAN_IP=192.0.2.12
